# The following are all bundled INSIDE npm itself
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/...), confirmed via direct
# filesystem inspection of the built image — not project dependencies
# (backend/package-lock.json has no "tar"/"brace-expansion"/"ip-address"
# entries reachable by `npm ci --only=production`).
# No fixed npm release available yet as of 2026-09-11.
# Risk accepted: only exercised by `npm install`/`npm ci` at image build
# time, never invoked by the running application.

# node-tar DoS via crafted long-path tar archive
CVE-2026-73566

# brace-expansion DoS via memory exhaustion in expand()
CVE-2026-14257

# brace-expansion DoS via unbounded intermediate arrays
CVE-2026-69152

# ip-address inconsistent parsing leading to SSRF
CVE-2026-69192
